# !! DO NOT TYPE A REAL VALUE INTO THIS FILE. It is committed and this repository is
# !! PUBLIC. The placeholders below are deliberately not blank, so that a value left
# !! unreplaced fails loudly instead of silently becoming an empty credential.
# !! Copy this file first; edit only the copy.
#
# TEMPLATE — committed. Copy it, do not edit it in place:
#
#   cd apps/production/email-stalwart/bulwark
#   cp env.secret.bulwark.example .env.secret.bulwark
#   $EDITOR .env.secret.bulwark               # paste the two values
#   ../../../../scripts/encrypt-env-files.sh apps/production/email-stalwart/bulwark
#
# Run that last command YOURSELF rather than asking the agent to. The agent must never
# create, read or write the real path: on 2026-08-29 two credentials were burned because
# the real file was in the agent's read-set and the harness reported the change including
# the secret line, even though the edit happened outside the agent's tools. The fix is
# structural — the agent writes the template, a human makes the copy.
#
# The copy is gitignored (`.env*`); only the `.encrypted` output is committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THESE ARE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# There is NO OAuth client secret here, and that is deliberate. Stalwart advertises PKCE
# S256 and a token endpoint auth method of "none", so Bulwark is registered as a public
# client (see OAuthClient in ../stalwart-config/plan.ndjson). A public client has no
# secret to hold, rotate, or leak.
#
# SESSION_SECRET encrypts remember-me sessions and the server-side per-user settings in
# the data volume. Changing it invalidates existing sessions and makes already-stored
# settings unreadable, so treat it as long-lived rather than something to rotate casually.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 48
SESSION_SECRET=<REPLACE-ME-openssl-rand-base64-48>

# Gates Bulwark's own admin dashboard, which is a separate thing from the Stalwart admin
# UI at admin.mail.activescott.com and from any mailbox account. Nobody signs in with this
# day to day; it exists so the dashboard is not open to whoever reaches the URL.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 24
ADMIN_PASSWORD=<REPLACE-ME-openssl-rand-base64-24>
